# Required: Base URL for the AWS API Gateway backend
REACT_APP_BASE_URL=https://your-api-id.execute-api.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com

# ── Bulk email (Resend / Brevo) ─────────────────────────────────────
# These are SERVER-ONLY env vars for the Vercel function api/send-bulk-email.js.
# Set them in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables),
# NOT as REACT_APP_* — they must never reach the browser bundle.
#
#   EMAIL_FROM       A verified sender, e.g. "HICC Gbagada <noreply@yourdomain.org>".
#   RESEND_API_KEY   Required to send via Resend.
#   BREVO_API_KEY    Required to send via Brevo.
#
# Optional:
#   EMAIL_PROVIDER       Default provider if the request omits one ("resend" | "brevo").
#   BACKEND_API_URL      AWS API base used to verify the caller's token
#                        (falls back to REACT_APP_BASE_URL).
#   AUTH_VERIFY_PATH     Admin-only GET path used to confirm the caller is an admin.
#   USER_VERIFY_PATH     Any-authenticated-user GET path used to confirm an
#                        allowlisted (non-admin) caller's token is genuine.
#   BULK_EMAIL_ALLOWLIST Extra login codes granted access, comma-separated.
#                        Defaults to "tolutrain,ayo". Keep in sync with
#                        src/utils/bulkEmailAccess.js.
#
# ── Email event webhook (Brevo/Resend → Supabase) ───────────────────
# Server-only env vars for the Vercel function api/email-webhook.js, which
# logs all email events into the Supabase `email_events` table
# (schema: db/email_events.sql).
#
#   SUPABASE_URL               Your Supabase project URL.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  Service role key (server-only; bypasses RLS).
#   EMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET       Shared secret included in the webhook URL, e.g.
#                              https://attendance.hiccgbagada.com/api/email-webhook?token=YOUR_SECRET
